# =============================================================================
# Data — downloaded, not authored
# =============================================================================
# The Kaggle dataset (~51MB) and everything model/refresh.py pulls from
# football-data.co.uk and ClubElo. All of it is reproducible:
#
#   curl -L -o model/data/raw.zip \
#     "https://www.kaggle.com/api/v1/datasets/download/adamgbor/club-football-match-data-2000-2025"
#   unzip -o model/data/raw.zip -d model/data && rm model/data/raw.zip
#
# See the README for the full setup steps.
model/data/*.csv
model/data/*.zip
model/data/live/

# Keep the directory itself, so the download above has somewhere to land.
!model/data/.gitkeep

# =============================================================================
# Trained artefacts — regenerate with `python model/train.py` (~50s)
# =============================================================================
# Deliberately not committed. These are binary blobs that change on every
# retrain, so committing them would add ~19MB to git history *per retrain*,
# permanently. They are fully reproducible from the data plus train.py.
#
#   model.pkl       the trained forest
#   state.pkl       team state from training
#   state_live.pkl  refreshed state, written by refresh.py
#   metrics.json    evaluation results
#   backtest.csv    per-match out-of-sample predictions (matched by *.csv above)
model/*.pkl
model/metrics.json

